# The oloid: the convex hull of two equal circles in perpendicular planes, held to its closed forms.
#
#   fieldform.exe --run benchmarks/smoke/oloid.ffc --keep-going --report oloid.json --exit
#
# Exit code 0 when every expect passed. Every line here is meant to succeed.
#
# With each circle through the other's centre (spread 1) the surface area is exactly that of a
# sphere of the circles' radius, 4*pi*r^2, and the volume is (2/3)*(2*E(3/4) + K(3/4))*r^3 =
# 3.05241847*r^3, E and K the complete elliptic integrals of parameter 3/4. It is three radii long
# and two across.
#   r = 20: volume 3.05241847 * 8000 = 24419.35, area 4*pi*400 = 5026.55
new
param name=R value=20
oloid 'roller' radius=R spread=1
expect target=roller volume=24419.35 tol=0.5%
expect target=roller area=5026.55 tol=0.5%
expect target=roller bbox=-30,-20,-20,30,20,20 tol=0.05

# --- The radius is a parameter and the spread is in radii, so halving the one halves the solid
# and leaves it an oloid: an eighth of the volume and a quarter of the area.
#   r = 10: volume 3052.42, area 1256.64
param name=R value=10
expect target=roller volume=3052.42 tol=0.5%
expect target=roller area=1256.64 tol=0.5%
expect target=roller bbox=-15,-10,-10,15,10,10 tol=0.05

# --- Turned, it is the same solid: the turn moves no volume.
oloid 'tipped' radius=10 spread=1 centre=60,0,0 turn=30,40,50
expect target=tipped volume=3052.42 tol=0.5%
expect target=tipped area=1256.64 tol=0.5%

# --- Other spreads are other solids of the same family, and no closed form is claimed for them
# but the box: the solid is (2 + spread) radii long whatever the spread. The square root of two
# is the roller whose centre of mass keeps its height.
#   r = 10, spread 1.41421356: -17.071 to 17.071 along X
oloid 'wide' radius=10 spread=1.41421356 centre=0,60,0
expect target=wide bbox=-17.071,50,-10,17.071,70,10 tol=0.05
